      "chunk_type": "text",
      "text": "Using Fibre Channel Switch Zoning\nThe following figure shows each connection to the host server(s) routed to an individual logical zone on the SAN. Two physical switches provide an alternate (redundant) data path to the storage array. If a single HBA, switch or RAID controller fails, the host server(s) can still access data on the storage array through one of the alternate paths provided by the switches.",
